{
  "repository": "sv5byp/FTFlow",
  "tag": "r155",
  "title": "FTflow r155 - Portable Windows x64",
  "body": "FTflow r155 is portable Windows x64 software for weak-signal digital communication on amateur radio bands, based on MSHV.\n\nFor an existing installation, use Help > Check for updates, or accept the startup update notification. The signed update automatically includes the clock synchronization companion, including when upgrading from an older updater. No separate download or manual file copying is required. Settings and contacts are kept.\n\nFor a first installation, download FTflow-SV5BYP-r155-Windows-x64-portable.zip, extract the complete ZIP into a folder on your hard disk and run FTFlow.exe. No setup or installer is required. Keep all included files and subfolders together.\n\nFor a manual upgrade, close FTflow and retain a backup, then copy FTFlow.exe, FTFlow-Update.exe and FTFlow-Time.exe into the existing permanent folder. Keep your settings and logs.\n\nThe source ZIP is for developers. FTFlow-update.bin and FTFlow-update.sig are used by the built-in updater. Ordinary users should use the in-program update or the Windows x64 portable ZIP.\n\nBased on MSHV, developed by Hrisimir Hristov, LZ2HV. Original contributor credits, map attribution and the GNU GPL license are retained.\n",
